WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.995 --> 00:00:13.656
was quite worried about his nose.

2
00:00:15.057 --> 00:00:17.818
He looked so silly that the Blue Fairy began to laugh.

3
00:00:17.838 --> 00:00:20.520
"Why are you laughing?"

4
00:00:21.081 --> 00:00:22.001
cried Pinocchio.

5
00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:25.864
"I am laughing at your lies," said the fairy.

6
00:00:25.884 --> 00:00:28.586
"It's easy to tell when you are lying.

7
00:00:29.346 --> 00:00:32.048
Your nose grows with every lie you tell."

8
00:00:33.456 --> 00:00:35.817
Ashamed, Pinocchio turned bright red.

9
00:00:35.837 --> 00:00:39.739
"I'm sorry," said Pinocchio.

10
00:00:39.759 --> 00:00:44.060
"I took the money from the marionette master.

11
00:00:45.261 --> 00:00:47.882
My father didn't know I went to the theater."

12
00:00:47.902 --> 00:00:53.304
"Do you promise to be a good boy and obey your father?"

13
00:00:53.985 --> 00:00:55.825
she asked before waving her wand.

14
00:00:56.546 --> 00:00:57.946
"Yes, I promise!"

15
00:00:58.586 --> 00:00:59.447
Pinocchio said.

16
00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:03.525
The Blue Fairy waved her wand, and a woodpecker appeared.

17
00:01:04.666 --> 00:01:06.387
It pecked his nose down to size.

18
00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.412
Then, the jail bars disappeared and Pinocchio climbed free.

19
00:01:13.432 --> 00:01:18.515
"This is the road that leads home," said the Blue Fairy, pointing.

20
00:01:18.535 --> 00:01:24.339
"If you stay on this road, you will reach Geppetto's home by nightfall.

21
00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:28.542
Remember your promise to be a good boy, Pinocchio!"

22
00:01:28.963 --> 00:01:30.504
she called, and she flew away.

23
00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:36.482
"Oh, what an awful thing it is to disobey our parents!

24
00:01:37.403 --> 00:01:43.706
From now on I will do whatever Geppetto asks," Pinocchio said as he walked down the road.

25
00:01:46.287 --> 00:01:48.989
A few hours later, Pinocchio began to get hungry.

26
00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:53.892
He saw a nearby grapevine and decided to ask the owner for some grapes.

27
00:01:54.872 --> 00:01:57.333
As he crossed the field, he fell into a trap.

28
00:01:58.474 --> 00:01:59.375
"Oh no!

29
00:01:59.975 --> 00:02:01.936
Someone, help me!"

30
00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:03.421
Pinocchio cried.

31
00:02:03.441 --> 00:02:08.823
"Aha, I have caught you," said the farmer, who was hiding.

32
00:02:08.843 --> 00:02:13.366
"So, you are the one who has been stealing my chickens."

33
00:02:14.646 --> 00:02:15.287
"No, sir.

34
00:02:15.687 --> 00:02:17.688
I have not stolen any chickens.

35
00:02:18.469 --> 00:02:23.511
Please, I was going to ask for some grapes because I am very hungry."

36
00:02:23.531 --> 00:02:28.214
"Aha! You were going to steal my grapes!

37
00:02:28.954 --> 00:02:31.115
I'll show you what we do with thieves!"

38
00:02:31.856 --> 00:02:32.276
he said.

39
00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:35.742
He pulled Pinocchio from the trap and took him home.

40
00:02:37.483 --> 00:02:41.084
When the farmer got home, he locked a chain around Pinocchio's neck.

41
00:02:41.104 --> 00:02:45.287
"My guard dog died this morning," said the farmer.

42
00:02:45.307 --> 00:02:49.609
"So tonight you will be a dog and guard my chicken coop.

43
00:02:50.229 --> 00:02:52.711
Tomorrow, I will decide how to punish you."

44
00:02:54.211 --> 00:02:55.012
Poor Pinocchio.

45
00:02:55.552 --> 00:02:58.874
He had tried to be a good boy, but the farmer didn't believe him.

46
00:03:00.635 --> 00:03:02.596
He was so hungry that he became tired.

47
00:03:03.668 --> 00:03:06.110
So, he crawled into the doghouse and fell asleep.

48
00:03:07.812 --> 00:03:11.195
Many hours passed, and Pinocchio heard voices nearby.

49
00:03:12.276 --> 00:03:13.817
He looked outside the doghouse.

50
00:03:14.498 --> 00:03:15.639
It was already night!

51
00:03:16.359 --> 00:03:18.421
He saw four weasels next to the chicken coop.

52
00:03:19.662 --> 00:03:20.543
"Who are you?"

53
00:03:20.944 --> 00:03:21.784
Pinocchio asked.

54
00:03:22.645 --> 00:03:23.246
They stopped.

55
00:03:23.266 --> 00:03:25.548
"Well, who are you?"

56
00:03:26.008 --> 00:03:27.169
one of the weasels asked.

57
00:03:27.189 --> 00:03:30.112
"And, where is our friend Oscar?"

58
00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:37.244
Pinocchio guessed that Oscar was the dog who had died, so he said, "Oscar died this morning.

59
00:03:37.964 --> 00:03:39.385
I am the new guard dog.

60
00:03:39.965 --> 00:03:40.706
Who are you?"

61
00:03:41.166 --> 00:03:42.367
Pinocchio asked again.

62
00:03:42.387 --> 00:03:48.350
"We are the weasels, and we are here to get dinner," said one of the weasels.

63
00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:50.731
"Oscar was our friend.

64
00:03:51.612 --> 00:03:55.134
I will make the same promise to you that I did to him.

65
00:03:56.695 --> 00:03:58.956
Every week, we would visit this coop.

66
00:03:59.808 --> 00:04:01.629
Oscar promised not to bark.

67
00:04:02.209 --> 00:04:06.711
So we would give one chicken to Oscar and take seven home for dinner.

68
00:04:07.652 --> 00:04:11.814
If you pretend to sleep, we will leave one chicken for you too."

69
00:04:14.055 --> 00:04:17.436
Before Pinocchio answered, the weasels snuck into the chicken coop.

70
00:04:18.377 --> 00:04:22.038
BAM! Pinocchio locked the door behind them and began to bark.

71
00:04:22.058 --> 00:04:24.259
"Woof, woof, woof!"

72
00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:25.220
he cried.

73
00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:29.803
The farmer ran down and found the weasels in the chicken coop.

74
00:04:31.144 --> 00:04:32.145
"Well done!"

75
00:04:32.565 --> 00:04:33.586
he said to Pinocchio.

76
00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:36.869
"You have caught the chicken thieves!

77
00:04:37.729 --> 00:04:39.871
Oscar must have been too old to hear them."

78
00:04:41.152 --> 00:04:44.495
Pinocchio didn't say anything about Oscar's promise to the weasels.

79
00:04:45.296 --> 00:04:46.036
He only nodded.

80
00:04:46.056 --> 00:04:51.501
"You have saved my chickens, so I will set you free," said the farmer.

81
00:04:51.521 --> 00:04:55.024
"But first, let me make you breakfast."

82
00:04:55.776 --> 00:04:58.901
Pinocchio nodded again, this time, with a big smile.
